# 2024红宝书考研英语超纲词
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 超纲词真题超纲汇总

aberration/ˌæbəˈreɪʃn/偏差；异常/This result is an aberration from the normal pattern.
abolish/əˈbɑːlɪʃ/废除/The government abolished the outdated law.
abstain/əbˈsteɪn/弃权；戒除/He abstained from voting on the issue.
acclaim/əˈkleɪm/称赞/The film received critical acclaim.
accrue/əˈkruː/积累/Interest accrues on the savings account.
acumen/əˈkjuːmən/敏锐/She has great business acumen.
adversary/ˈædvərseri/对手/He defeated his adversary in the debate.
aesthetic/esˈθetɪk/美学的/The building has great aesthetic appeal.
affinity/əˈfɪnəti/亲和力/She has an affinity for mathematics.
allegation/ˌæləˈɡeɪʃn/指控/The allegations against him were proven false.
alleviate/əˈliːvieɪt/缓解/The medicine helped alleviate the pain.
amalgamate/əˈmælɡəmeɪt/合并/The two companies amalgamated to form a larger entity.
ameliorate/əˈmiːliəreɪt/改善/The new policy aims to ameliorate working conditions.
analogous/əˈnæləɡəs/类似的/The situation is analogous to what happened last year.
anarchy/ˈænərki/无政府状态/The country descended into anarchy after the coup.
anecdote/ˈænɪkdoʊt/轶事/He told an amusing anecdote about his childhood.
annihilate/əˈnaɪəleɪt/消灭/The bomb could annihilate an entire city.
anomaly/əˈnɑːməli/异常/The test result was an anomaly.
antagonism/ænˈtæɡənɪzəm/对抗/There is deep antagonism between the two groups.
anthropology/ˌænθrəˈpɑːlədʒi/人类学/She studied anthropology at university.
apathy/ˈæpəθi/冷漠/Voter apathy is a problem in many countries.
apprehension/ˌæprɪˈhenʃn/忧虑；逮捕/She felt apprehension about the future.
arbitrary/ˈɑːrbrɪteri/任意的/The decision seemed completely arbitrary.
archaic/ɑːrˈkeɪɪk/过时的/The law is archaic and needs to be updated.
arduous/ˈɑːrdʒuəs/艰苦的/The journey to the summit was arduous.
aristocracy/ˌærɪˈstɑːkrəsi/贵族/The aristocracy controlled most of the land.
articulate/ɑːrˈtɪkjuleɪt/清晰表达/She articulated her vision for the company.
aspire/əˈspaɪər/渴望/He aspires to become a great musician.
atrocity/əˈtrɑːsəti/暴行/The atrocities committed during the war shocked the world.
audit/ˈɔːdɪt/审计/The company underwent an external audit.
austerity/ɔːˈsterəti/紧缩/The government introduced austerity measures.
authenticity/ˌɔːθenˈtɪsəti/真实性/The painting's authenticity was confirmed.
avert/əˈvɜːrt/避免/Quick action averted a disaster.
benevolent/bəˈnevələnt/仁慈的/He is a benevolent leader who cares about his people.
bureaucracy/bjʊˈrɑːkrəsi/官僚机构/The bureaucracy slowed down the approval process.
calibrate/ˈkælɪbreɪt/校准/You need to calibrate the instrument before use.
catalyst/ˈkætəlɪst/催化剂/Her speech was a catalyst for change.
catastrophe/kəˈtæstrəfi/灾难/The earthquake was a catastrophe for the region.
chronological/ˌkrɑːnəˈlɑːdʒɪkl/按时间顺序的/Please arrange the events in chronological order.
circumscribe/ˈsɜːrkəmskraɪb/限制/Freedom of speech is circumscribed by law.
coerce/koʊˈɜːrs/胁迫/He was coerced into signing the document.
coherent/koʊˈhɪrənt/连贯的/She presented a coherent argument.
collaborate/kəˈlæbəreɪt/合作/The two departments collaborated on the project.
commemorate/kəˈmeməreɪt/纪念/The monument commemorates the fallen soldiers.
compatible/kəmˈpætəbl/兼容的/The software is compatible with most systems.
compel/kəmˈpel/强迫/The evidence compelled him to confess.
complacent/kəmˈpleɪsnt/自满的/Don't become complacent about your success.
comply/kəmˈplaɪ/遵守/All employees must comply with the regulations.
concede/kənˈsiːd/承认/He conceded that he was wrong.
